<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Free City of Danzig (1807-1814)</h1><p class="st-meta">1807 CE – 1814 CE · capital Danzig</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Napoleonic city-state created at Tilsit, nominally free but in practice a French fortress on the Baltic.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> created the Free City of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gdansk">Danzig</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaties-of-tilsit">Treaty of Tilsit</a> in 1807, taking the city and its surrounding territory from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-prussia">Kingdom of Prussia</a>. It was placed under the joint protection of Prussia and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-saxony">Kingdom of Saxony</a>, whose king also ruled the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-warsaw">Duchy of Warsaw</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The city had a senate and its own constitution, but real power lay with the French governor, General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-rapp">Jean Rapp</a>, and a large garrison. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/continental-system">Continental System</a> cut off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gdansk">Danzig</a>'s trade with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> and ruined its merchants, while the city had to pay heavy contributions. It served as a base for the 1812 invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1813 Russian and Prussian forces besieged the city for most of the year, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-rapp">Rapp</a> surrendered at the end of 1813, the garrison leaving in January 1814. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> returned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gdansk">Danzig</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1815.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/free-city-of-danzig-1807-1814.jpg" alt="Free City of Danzig (1807-1814)" width="320" height="215"><figcaption>Image: Mnmazur · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Free_City_of_Danzig.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1807 CE – 1814 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Danzig</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jean Rapp</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheran Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Napoleonic Free City of Danzig, Republic of Danzig</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1810&amp;focus=free-city-of-danzig-1807-1814" aria-label="Free City of Danzig (1807-1814) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5092 314 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Free City of Danzig (1807-1814) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5412 570L5054 728M5412 570L5300 622"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M5300 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5412 570h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5412 570h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1810&amp;focus=free-city-of-danzig-1807-1814">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
